From: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] b43: fix two RF control override value masks on N-PHY rev 7

Two entries of tbl_rf_control_override_rev7_over1 carry a value mask that
does not match their own shift: field 0x0100 has mask 0x0100 with shift
11, and field 0x0200 has mask 0x0800 with shift 12. Every other entry of
the three rev 7 tables has the mask covering exactly the field its shift
lands in.

brcmsmac has the two masks one place further along, (0x1 << 11) for field
0x0100 and (0x1 << 12) for field 0x0200, and an MMIO capture of wl
6.30.102.7 on a BCM6362 (N-PHY rev 8, radio 2057 rev 8) agrees with
brcmsmac: the setup of the PAPD calibration programs both fields, and the
two modify operations it produces on 0x0340 carry mask 0x0800 and 0x1000.

The effect is not confined to the bit that does not get written.
b43_nphy_rf_ctl_override_rev7() clears the value mask and ORs the shifted
value in, so for field 0x0100 it clears bit 8 of 0x0340 - which belongs
to the low pass filter bandwidth field, mask 0x0700, that the same
sequence programs a few operations earlier - and sets bit 11 regardless.
Whether that destroys the bandwidth depends on its value: on the captured
channel it does not, because there bit 8 is already clear.

Verified: records #11800-#11805, from
"PHY.OR   addr=0x0342 val=0x0100 (set 0x0100)"
Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmsmac/phy/phy_n.c?id=848acc8ffe1b#n14969
Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmsmac/phy/phy_n.c?id=848acc8ffe1b#n14977
Link: https://github.com/aleferri/b43-6362-wip/blob/a54f82b/router-data/dsl-3580l/opinit-ch1-ch6-bw20.decoded

Signed-off-by: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/tables_nphy.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/tables_nphy.c
@@ -3224,8 +3224,8 @@ static const struct nphy_rf_control_override_rev7
 	{ 0x0080, 0x340, 0x341, 0x0700, 8 },
 	{ 0x0800, 0x340, 0x341, 0x4000, 14 },
 	{ 0x0400, 0x340, 0x341, 0x2000, 13 },
-	{ 0x0200, 0x340, 0x341, 0x0800, 12 },
-	{ 0x0100, 0x340, 0x341, 0x0100, 11 },
+	{ 0x0200, 0x340, 0x341, 0x1000, 12 },
+	{ 0x0100, 0x340, 0x341, 0x0800, 11 },
 	{ 0x0040, 0x340, 0x341, 0x0040, 6 },
 	{ 0x0001, 0x340, 0x341, 0x0001, 0 },
 };
